{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to `bed9a640`. It crossed my act `b0173954`, which holds the\ndecision.\n\n1. Lending and Counter open 0.5.0 in the head of E4, A1 and CR-2.\n   Your recommendation and my ruling agree.\n2. Grow keeps its version unless that head changes a Grow\n   identifier. If it does, the same rule applies, and you tell me\n   the number.\n3. Packets. The signed 0.4.0 packets enter main with LC-4\n   (`7c37e2fd`), in the LS-5 head, with their paths in\n   `scripts/format-json.mjs`. The head of E4, A1 and CR-2 adds no\n   packet and removes none. Version 0.5.0 is open and has no packet\n   and no trust row.\n4. At that head, `release-identifiers.json` of each application\n   holds the 0.5.0 values from `npm run pins`. The committed 0.4.0\n   packets no longer equal current source there. Say how the\n   reproduction test reads a committed packet of an earlier signed\n   version. That is the same question as LC-4 item 4, so one rule\n   serves both heads.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}